cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use osqf-archive (code, derived notes or index), please cite it as
  below. Credit for each talk belongs to its speaker; cite the talk itself
  when you rely on what it says.
type: software
title: "osqf-archive: a searchable archive of osQF / R-in-finance conference talks, 2009-2026"
abstract: >-
  Derived notes, embeddings, an entity graph and an MCP server over eighteen
  years of publicly posted osQF / R-in-finance conference talks, built end to
  end with local open-weight models. An independent, unofficial project: not
  affiliated with or endorsed by the osQF conference.
authors:
  - family-names: Jakel
    given-names: Travis S.
version: "0.2"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/travisjakel/osqf-archive"
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - quantitative finance
  - OCR
  - model context protocol
  - R
references:
  - type: unpublished
    title: "Text, OCR, or Pixels? A Retrieval Decision Matrix for Quant-Finance Documents, Built on Eighteen Years of the osQF Archive"
    authors:
      - family-names: Jakel
        given-names: Travis S.
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/travisjakel/osqf-archive/blob/main/docs/paper.pdf"
